of every objective constraint; Section 3 shows the structural failure.</p>
<h2>Reproducibility and revision boundary</h2>
<p>This revision reads saved results, existing source and worker logs. It does not retrain, retune, recompute held-out metrics, generate new UMAP coordinates
or change machine verdicts. Original generated dataset reports are retained. A pre-revision report is preserved locally; current numeric claims map to
saved artifacts in the claim-source file.</p>
<p>Source, objectives, configurations, environment locks and manifests identify the executed workflow. Shared raw data, tile features, checkpoints and
pathology weights/derivatives are not redistributed. All downstream files remain inside Agent3. No external LLM was used in the reproducible analysis
or templated reporting core.</p>
</div>
